# OS
.DS_Store

# Credentials and local state. Shunkan keeps all of this in ~/.shunkan by
# default, well outside the repo, but belt and braces: if anyone ever points
# SHUNKAN_HOME at the working tree these patterns stop a broker token or a
# market-data cache from being committed. Zerodha's API terms also prohibit
# redistributing their data, so the store never belongs in git.
#
# Anchor these to the repo root with a leading slash. An unanchored `store/`
# also matches src/shunkan/store/, which is a source package, and silently
# drops it from the repo. CI caught that; a local editable install did not.
credentials.json
*.token
.env
.env.*
/.shunkan/
/store/
/cache/
*.parquet
/portfolio.json
/watchlist.json
/alerts.json
